# Keep Resume Repo in Sync

This project (`armindashti.github.io`) and the resume repo are a **paired pair**. Do not finish a change here without updating the resume repo.

## Resume repo

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Path | `C:/Users/armin/GitHub/resume` |
| Role | Source / CV twin of this personal site |

## Required workflow

1. Make the change in this repo as requested.
2. Apply the **same intent** in `C:/Users/armin/GitHub/resume` (content, design, metadata, assets, or structure as applicable).
3. Adapt to resume layout differences (`index_EN.html`, `index_FA.html`, assets, etc.) — do not blind-copy paths that do not exist there.
4. Treat the task as incomplete until both repos reflect the change.
5. Do not commit or push either repo unless the user explicitly asks.

## What counts as a change

Any edit that affects the published site or its maintainability: HTML, CSS, images, SEO files, `metadata.json`, README, and similar.

## Exceptions

- Cursor-only / agent config under `.cursor/` that has no user-facing resume equivalent — still check whether resume needs a matching rule or note; skip only when there is nothing to mirror.
- Pure git/tooling ops that do not alter project content (status, log) — no resume update required.

## Examples

```text
// ❌ BAD — change style.css here and stop
// ✅ GOOD — update style here, then update matching styles/markup in resume (EN + FA as needed)

// ❌ BAD — add a new job to index.html only
// ✅ GOOD — add the same experience to resume HTML (and PDF only if the user asked for PDF)
```
